{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And every sin-offering whose blood is brought, etc.</b> <b>to make atonement in the holy.</b> Now the place of the curtain is called \"holy,\" for the courtyard — if it is holy relative to the Tent of Meeting, it is profane. And behold, that which is inside the curtain is also called \"holy, relative to the Tent of Meeting,\" as in \"Thus shall Aaron come into the holy\" (Leviticus 16:3). And this sin-offering is the sin-offering of the high priest or the congregation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:52.553712564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}